# drainmod7_soildata_ssurgo_builder.py
#
# First-pass DRAINMOD 7 soil builder from SSURGO/SDA.
#
# Purpose:
#   Build one soil file set per pixel using the stations CSV generated by the
#   DRAINMOD 7 weather script, following the structure of the native Larson files:
#       - .DMN  -> physical-chemical layer properties and links to MIS/WDV
#       - .MIS  -> multi-layer soil water characteristic file
#       - .SIN  -> representative soil water characteristic + Green-Ampt + upflux
#       - .WDV  -> water-table / volume-drained file
#
# Design choices:
#   1. Use the same layer boundaries and head grid as a working template MIS file.
#   2. Use SSURGO to derive water contents for each layer:
#         theta_s      from porosity ~= 1 - bulk_density / 2.65
#         theta_330    from wthirdbar_r / 100
#         theta_15000  from wfifteenbar_r / 100
#      and interpolate onto the template head grid.
#   3. Build the SIN SWCC from the top template layer using the same head grid as
#      the working SIN template.
#   4. Copy the Green-Ampt A/B table and the final SIN upflux table from the
#      working SIN template.
#   5. Build WDV by scaling each template layer's cumulative drained volume by the
#      ratio of drainable porosity:
#         (theta_s - theta_330)_SSURGO / (theta_s - theta_330)_template
#      This preserves the native file structure while allowing SSURGO to change
#      the amount of drainable water by layer.
#
# This is meant to be a conservative Illinois-ready starting point, not a final
# calibration workflow.
#
# Outputs:
#   - DMN/<pixel_id>.DMN
#   - MIS/<pixel_id>.MIS
#   - SIN/<pixel_id>.SIN
#   - WDV/<pixel_id>.WDV
#   - drainmod7_soil_map_<area>.csv
#   - drainmod7_soil_summary_<area>.csv
#   - mukey_samples_<area>.csv
#   - mukey_frequency_report_<area>.csv
#   - issues_<area>.csv

